//    standalone formula.
// 4. Speculative look-ahead (SpeculativeConstrainedRollout with 2 steps) when
//    IsCompletePrefix fires: if a longer complete expression is reachable, keep
//    generating inside the span instead of closing immediately. This nudges
//    "<<n * frac_1>>" toward "<<n * frac_1 * frac_2>>".
// 5. CloseConstrainedSpan used directly when no speculative extension is viable
//    (budget-safe, avoids per-span budget over-spending from attempt 62).
// 6. Force-open at budget pressure (≤4 steps) to always emit a final span.
